From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] evr: mixer video processor, alpha bitmap, position mapper, quality advise, clock sink, substream input types

The default video mixer (MFCreateVideoMixer) had these as E_NOTIMPL stubs:

- IMFVideoProcessor: GetVideoProcessorMode/SetVideoProcessorMode (S_FALSE with a
  null GUID until a mode is chosen, S_OK afterwards; the mode must be one the
  device offers, E_INVALIDARG otherwise, and the processor is created again with
  it), GetProcAmpRange/Get/SetProcAmpValues (brightness, contrast, hue,
  saturation: ranges, defaults 0/1/0/1, E_INVALIDARG for unknown flags or out of
  range values, all or nothing), GetFilteringRange/GetFilteringValue/
  SetFilteringValue (the twelve noise and detail filter properties). Every one
  is MF_E_TRANSFORM_TYPE_NOT_SET until the input and output types are set, and
  E_POINTER for a NULL out parameter.
- IMFVideoMixerBitmap: SetAlphaBitmap (validates the parameters, keeps the
  surface, documented defaults for parameters that are not flagged),
  UpdateAlphaBitmapParameters (only the flagged members), GetAlphaBitmapParameters
  and UpdateAlphaBitmapParameters are MF_E_NOT_INITIALIZED without a bitmap,
  ClearAlphaBitmap.
- IMFVideoPositionMapper::MapOutputCoordinateToInputStream: maps through the
  input stream's output rectangle, MF_E_INVALIDINDEX for unknown streams.
- IMFQualityAdvise (mixer): the mixer cannot drop or degrade, so only "none" and
  "normal" are accepted (MF_E_NO_MORE_DROP_MODES, MF_E_NO_MORE_QUALITY_LEVELS,
  E_INVALIDARG out of range), DropTime is MF_E_DROPTIME_NOT_SUPPORTED.
- IMFClockStateSink (mixer): the five notifications are S_OK and the state and
  rate are kept.
- SetInputType for a substream: validated against the device, kept per stream,
  and no longer clears the reference stream's and the output type; an unknown
  stream is MF_E_INVALIDSTREAMNUMBER.
- GetInputAvailableType, GetOutputStreamAttributes and ProcessEvent keep
  answering E_NOTIMPL (what the conformance tests show), without the FIXME.

The conformance tests' todo_wine marks that pass now are removed.
The alpha bitmap is stored and validated; the mixer does not blend it yet.
